  "problem": {
    "id": "train-228",
    "question": "A company has 200 employees.  60% of the employees drive to work.  Of the employees who don't drive to work, half take public transportation. How many more employees drive to work than take public transportation?",
    "gold": "40",
    "answer": "Drive to work:200(.60)=<<200*.60=120>>120\nDon't Drive to work:200-120=<<200-120=80>>80\nPublic Transportation:80(.50)=40 employees\n80-40=<<80-40=40>>40 employees\n#### 40"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many more employees drive to work than take public transportation, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the number of employees who drive to work.\n2. Calculate the number of employees who do not drive to work.\n3. Determine how many of the employees who do not drive to work take public transportation.\n4. Find the difference between the number of employees who drive to work and the number of employees who take public transportation.\n\nLet's start with the first step:\n\n1. Calculate the number of employees who drive to work.\n   The company has 200 employees, and 60% of them drive to work.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of employees who drive to work} = 0.60 \\times 200 = 120\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate the number of employees who do not drive to work.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of employees who do not drive to work} = 200 - 120 = 80\n   \\]\n\n3. Determine how many of the employees who do not drive to work take public transportation.\n   Half of the employees who do not drive to work take public transportation.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of employees who take public transportation} = \\frac{80}{2} = 40\n   \\]\n\n4. Find the difference between the number of employees who drive to work and the number of employees who take public transportation.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Difference} = 120 - 40 = 80\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of employees who drive to work is 80 more than the number of employees who take public transportation. The final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{80}\n\\]",
